---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ObfuscatedEmail from "../../components/ObfuscatedEmail.astro";
// NOTE: this page gets run through Staticrypt as a post-build step before publishing —
// it should never ship un-encrypted. See build/deploy notes.
---
<BaseLayout title="Deposit Instructions" description="Deposit instructions for screened clients." noindex={true}>
  <section>
    <h1>Deposit Instructions</h1>
    <p class="drop-cap">
      I'm glad we've gotten this far. Below are my detailed instructions for making a deposit, but if you
      have questions, don't hesitate to ask. It's better to ask than make a mistake that could shut down
      these options for everyone.
    </p>
    <p>
      I confirm deposits within 24hrs of you sending them. If more than 24hrs has passed and you haven't
      heard back, something might have gone awry, particularly with electronic deposits.
    </p>
    <p>
      YouPay/Cashapp/Zelle/Vanilla Visa are preferred. You can split the deposit among the methods if you
      wish — just let me know. You have several options below, and two additional ones if you're
      established. YouPay allows you to use your credit cards safely and discreetly, though they charge a
      processing fee to stay in business.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you wish to prepay in full, please make sure that transaction is finished/submitted at least
      48hrs prior to our meeting. I'll need to be able to confirm receipt and troubleshoot if there are
      issues (banks are overly concerned about security).
    </p>
    <p>
      Once established, you have the option of direct credit card payment, or cash [discreetly]
      overnighted to my business mailing address. Since these options are directly connected to my actual
      business, they're offered at my discretion.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="callout">
    <p>
      Please use the email address below — do <strong>not</strong> use my regular email address for
      emailed gift cards, of any kind.
    </p>
    <p>Please copy and paste my alternate email address, not associated with this website (yes, that's with two Cs):</p>
    <ObfuscatedEmail user="ac" domain="accreativerva.com" />
    <p class="rules">
      Feel free to use my initials [A.C.] if you need to fill in a name, and do not include a message. If
      you feel you must, do not allude to any type of meeting, do not use the word "deposit," and do not
      include calendar dates. Referring to photography is ideal but not required. The less said, the better.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Featured method: full-width, title/content split, gold accent bar — matches
       the .callout treatment above. Bitcoin gets the same treatment below. -->
  <section class="deposit-featured">
    <h2>YouPay.me</h2>
    <div class="deposit-featured-body">
      <p>
        You can use your regular credit card on the YouPay site. Go to
        {" "}<a href="https://youpay.me/AvainRVA804" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">my profile</a>{" "}
        , choose the Cash Gifts Wishlist (the one with a photo of money), choose the appropriate gift,
        and check out. I'm still filling out my profile and gifts, so more options will appear with time.
        I also have the ability to create a custom amount and send the link directly to you, if needed.
      </p>
      <p class="rules">
        Feel free to use my initials [A.C.] if you need to fill in a name, and do not include a message. If
        you feel you must, do not allude to any type of meeting, do not use the word "deposit," and do not
        include calendar dates.
      </p>
      <p>If something in the process confuses you, don't proceed — choose a simpler method that you understand. Please don't create issues for everyone else who enjoys the convenience.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="deposit-grid">
    <article class="deposit-card">
      <h3>Cashapp</h3>
      <p>If you already have and use Cashapp, you can send me the deposit or full amount via the app.</p>
      <p><strong>My address is:</strong> @ACcreative</p>
      <p>Please let me know if you're sending it this way so I know to look for it.</p>
      <p class="rules">
        Feel free to use my initials [A.C.] if you need to fill in a name, and do not include a message. If
        you feel you must, do not allude to any type of meeting, do not use the word "deposit," and do not
        include calendar dates.
      </p>
      <p>FYI: I confirm receipt via email, not in app.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="deposit-card">
      <h3>Vanilla Visa — Option 1 (emailed gift card)</h3>
      <p>
        This is an emailed gift card. Please purchase only from the
        {" "}<a href="https://www.vanillagift.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">official website</a>{" "}
        — I cannot guarantee the authenticity of any other source. Follow the emailed gift card
        instructions above, using the email address on this page.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="deposit-card">
      <h3>Vanilla Visa — Option 2 (physical card)</h3>
      <p>
        Purchase a physical Vanilla Visa gift card in a store with cash (no electronic trail for
        you!). Remove the cardboard packaging and any stickers, and photograph the front and back of
        the card. Email me the photos — make sure nothing obstructs the card number, expiration date,
        or security code.
      </p>
      <p><a href="https://www.vanillagift.com/help/where-to-buy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Store locator</a></p>
    </article>

    <article class="deposit-card">
      <h3>Zelle</h3>
      <p>If you'd like to make a bank transfer using Zelle, it's quite easy — please use the email address on this page.</p>
      <p class="rules">
        Feel free to use my initials [A.C.] if you need to fill in a name, and do not include a message. If
        you feel you must, do not allude to any type of meeting, do not use the word "deposit," and do not
        include calendar dates.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="deposit-card">
      <h3>Amazon — Option 1 (emailed gift card)</h3>
      <p>Use the emailed gift card instructions above, with the email address on this page.</p>
      <p class="rules">
        Feel free to use my initials [A.C.] if you need to fill in a name, and do not include a message. If
        you feel you must, do not allude to any type of meeting, do not use the word "deposit," and do not
        include calendar dates.
      </p>
      <p>Amazon is for deposits only, not for paying the full balance — use one of the other options for that.</p>
      <p><a href="#" class="link-todo">Amazon emailed gift cards</a></p>
      <!-- TODO(Toni): couldn't verify Amazon's official e-gift-card URL — their robots.txt blocks
           every path I tried, so I didn't want to guess on a payment-adjacent link. Since you
           already have this link live on the WP page, easiest is just pasting it to me. -->
    </article>

    <article class="deposit-card">
      <h3>Amazon — Option 2 (physical card)</h3>
      <p>
        Find physical Amazon gift cards in any store. Purchase with cash, remove packaging and
        stickers, and photograph the back of the card with the gift code visible in full. If the code
        is under a scratch-off coating, be careful not to scratch off the code itself.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <section class="deposit-featured">
    <h2>Bitcoin / BTC</h2>
    <div class="deposit-featured-body deposit-featured-body--split">
      <div class="deposit-featured-text">
        <p>
          In case you're wondering, I use Bitcoin to pay for advertising — I'm not investing in
          crypto or NFTs. My Bitcoin wallet QR code (currently Blue Wallet) is below.
        </p>
        <p>
          Because of the inevitable changes in laws regarding crypto purchases, a simple tutorial
          isn't enough to cover what a first-time or anonymity-minded user needs to know. However,
          if you already know what you're doing and use BTC, you're welcome to pay the deposit that
          way.
        </p>
      </div>
      <!-- Drop the real QR code image at /public/images/btc-wallet-qr.jpg and swap the placeholder
           div below for: <img src="/images/btc-wallet-qr.jpg" alt="Bitcoin wallet QR code" class="deposit-qr-image" /> -->
      <div class="deposit-qr">
        <div class="deposit-qr-placeholder" aria-hidden="true">QR code</div>
        <p class="deposit-qr-caption">[Drop the real QR image at /public/images/btc-wallet-qr.jpg]</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta">
    <h2>Thank you so much!</h2>
    <p>I appreciate your trust, and we'll be meeting soon.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .callout {
    background: var(--color-surface-alt);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent-gold);
    padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
  }
  .rules { font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--color-text-muted); }
  .cta { text-align: center; margin-top: 2rem; }

  /* --- featured panels: YouPay + Bitcoin, full-width, title/content split with a
     gold accent bar (same idiom as .callout above, for consistency within this page). --- */
  .deposit-featured {
    background: var(--color-surface-alt);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent-gold);
    padding: 1.5rem 1.75rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(9rem, 14rem) 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .deposit-featured h2 { margin: 0; }
  .deposit-featured-body p:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .deposit-featured-body p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .deposit-featured-body--split {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    gap: 2rem;
    align-items: start;
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .deposit-featured,
    .deposit-featured-body--split {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  /* --- the six standard methods: a real grid, DOM order = visual order (no CSS
     `order` used anywhere), so reading order and tab order both stay exactly as
     written — collapses to one column on narrow screens without reshuffling. --- */
  .deposit-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }
  .deposit-card {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding: 1.25rem 1.25rem 1.5rem;
  }
  .deposit-card h3 { font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 0 0 0.6rem; }
  .deposit-card p { font-size: 0.9rem; margin: 0 0 0.6rem; }
  .deposit-card p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .deposit-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }

  /* --- QR code slot --- */
  .deposit-qr {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    width: 10rem;
  }
  .deposit-qr-placeholder {
    width: 10rem;
    height: 10rem;
    background: repeating-linear-gradient(135deg, var(--cream) 0px, var(--cream) 2px, var(--warm-off-white) 2px, var(--warm-off-white) 40px);
    border: 1px dashed var(--color-border);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }
  .deposit-qr-image { width: 10rem; height: 10rem; display: block; }
  .deposit-qr-caption {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    text-align: center;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Visible marker for links needing a real URL — impossible to miss, easy to grep for. */
  .link-todo {
    color: var(--color-accent-gold);
    text-decoration: underline wavy;
  }
</style>
